Begin with the central distinction: a coordinate chart can report superunit motion while the velocity relative to the shifted local frame remains bounded by light speed. Background on [spacetime](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spacetime) and [Lorentzian manifolds](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lorentzian_manifold) can help orient new readers.

